sequenceDiagram
    autonumber
    title HackMatch — US-022: Confirm and Lock a Team Roster — Transaction Sequence
    actor TeamLead
    participant ReactUI
    participant ExpressAPI
    participant LockService as Lock Validation<br/>and Service
    participant PostgreSQL

    TeamLead->>ReactUI: Open owned team workspace
    ReactUI->>ExpressAPI: GET /api/teams/:teamId/lock/validate
    ExpressAPI->>ExpressAPI: Verify Firebase token, MFA, active verified PART, and ownership
    alt Unauthorized or invalid team
        ExpressAPI-->>ReactUI: 400, 401, 403, or 404
        ReactUI-->>TeamLead: Keep prior roster and show protected error
    else Authorized owner
        ExpressAPI->>LockService: Validate current roster without mutation
        LockService->>PostgreSQL: Read team, confirmed members, vacancies, and compatibility data
        PostgreSQL-->>LockService: Status, lock time, member count, and open slots
        LockService-->>ExpressAPI: canLock, reasons, bounds, and permitted member display
        ExpressAPI-->>ReactUI: Loading, eligible, blocked, empty, or retry state
        ReactUI-->>TeamLead: Review roster and Confirm & Lock action
    end

    TeamLead->>ReactUI: Confirm irreversible lock
    ReactUI->>ExpressAPI: POST /api/teams/:teamId/lock
    ExpressAPI->>ExpressAPI: Recheck authentication, active account, role, and ownership
    ExpressAPI->>LockService: lockTeam for authenticated owner
    LockService->>PostgreSQL: lock_team RPC
    PostgreSQL->>PostgreSQL: Acquire target-team advisory lock shared with join and leave
    PostgreSQL->>PostgreSQL: Lock team row and recheck owner plus Open status
    PostgreSQL->>PostgreSQL: Count confirmed members and validate roster bounds
    PostgreSQL->>PostgreSQL: Legacy shadow-event lifecycle, bounds, and event-membership checks
    alt Invalid, underfilled, overfilled, already locked, or concurrent winner
        PostgreSQL-->>LockService: Domain conflict with no transaction writes
        LockService-->>ExpressAPI: Explicit 409 code and current details
        ExpressAPI-->>ReactUI: Lock rejected
        ReactUI-->>TeamLead: Preserve roster, close stale confirmation, and revalidate
    else Eligible roster commits
        PostgreSQL->>PostgreSQL: Set recruitment_status Locked and server locked_at
        PostgreSQL->>PostgreSQL: Cancel team Pending invitations and applications
        PostgreSQL->>PostgreSQL: Persist cancellation alerts and locked-roster member alerts
        PostgreSQL-->>LockService: Lock timestamp, member bounds, and canceled count
        LockService->>PostgreSQL: Reload canonical team view
        PostgreSQL-->>LockService: Locked roster and lifecycle
        LockService-->>ExpressAPI: Successful lock result
        ExpressAPI-->>ReactUI: 200 Locked team, timestamp, and cancellation summary
        ReactUI-->>TeamLead: Show Locked badge and disable recruitment and mutation controls
    end

    Note over PostgreSQL: Join, approval, acceptance, and leave serialize through the target-team advisory lock or team row lock. A loser observes the committed roster state and no partial Locked plus underfilled result should commit.
    Note over LockService,PostgreSQL: Current code still reads Internal Shadow Event status, end date, min/max size, and per-event membership. The Event-Free target is an active unlocked team with 2–4 confirmed members and per-team uniqueness.
    Note over ReactUI,ExpressAPI: No event is selected for locking. Team response models still expose eventId and internal participant identifiers that the lock UI does not require.

